---
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ResultsCard from '../components/ResultsCard.astro';
import CommandBlock from '../components/CommandBlock.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import {counts,cloneCommands,markdown,readme,section,domains} from '../lib/content';
import {home,exam,results} from '../lib/images';
import {href,repository,canonical} from '../lib/urls';
const platforms=await markdown(section(readme,'Supported platforms'));
const comparison=await markdown(section(readme,'How it compares'));
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'SoftwareApplication',name:'autorelabel',applicationCategory:'EducationalApplication',operatingSystem:'Linux x86_64',description:'Timed RHCSA and RHCE practice exams on real RHEL 10 virtual machines, graded after every node reboots.',url:canonical('/'),license:`${repository}/blob/main/LICENSE`,codeRepository:repository};
const features=[
  ['An exam-like start','Configure node1’s network from the console. Reset node2’s unknown root password. Set up the repositories. RHCE starts with an empty project directory.'],
  ['Method-agnostic grading','The final state counts. Use UUID or LABEL, nmcli or keyfiles. The grader never looks at the commands you typed.'],
  ['Every task self-tested','Untouched labs, reference solutions, accepted alternatives, and classic mistakes are checked on real RHEL 10 VMs with libvirt and VirtualBox.'],
  ['Full objective coverage',`All ${domains.rhcsa.reduce((n,d)=>n+d.objectives.length,0)} RHCSA and ${domains.rhce.reduce((n,d)=>n+d.objectives.length,0)} RHCE objective lines have at least two tasks. ${counts.practice} tasks are available only in practice.`],
  ['A fixed difficulty mix','Every exam has 6 easy tasks at 10 points, 8 medium at 15, and 6 hard at 20. The total is always 300.'],
  ['A clock that survives your host','A background proctor keeps the clock. With the default settings, time while your computer sleeps or is off does not count.'],
  ['RHCE, with the real tools','ansible-core, the RHEL system roles, an offline execution environment, ansible-navigator, and VS Code in your browser.'],
  ['A clean uninstall','A ledger records every resource. The uninstaller removes what autorelabel created, including a rescue copy if the repository is gone.'],
];
---
<Layout title="Graded after a reboot" description="Free, open-source RHCSA and RHCE practice exams on real RHEL 10 VMs. 20 tasks, a timed exam, and grading after every node reboots." schema={schema}>
<main id="content">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Graded after<br/><em>a reboot.</em></h1><p>Take a timed RHCSA or RHCE practice exam on real RHEL 10 VMs, then see what survives.</p><div class="exam-tags"><span>RHCSA (EX200)</span><span>RHCE (EX294)</span></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href={href('/start/')} data-magnetic data-cursor="open">Get started <Icon name="arrow"/></a><a class="text-link" href={repository} data-cursor="GitHub ↗">View on GitHub ↗</a></div><CommandBlock id="home-clone" commands={cloneCommands} chip/><p class="host-note">Linux x86_64 · your RHEL 10 ISO · no subscription</p></div><ResultsCard id="reboot-result"/></div></section>
  <section class="facts room--night" aria-label="The facts"><div class="container facts__inner"><div class="fact"><span class="mono" data-count={counts.total}>{counts.total}</span><p>tasks in the bank<span>{counts.rhcsa} RHCSA · {counts.rhce} RHCE</span></p></div><div class="fact"><span class="mono">2×</span><p>every objective line<span>At least two tasks per line</span></p></div><div class="fact"><Icon name="reboot"/><p>Graded after a reboot<span>Only persistent configuration counts</span></p></div></div></section>
  <section class="exam-process" id="exam-process"><div class="container"><div class="process-heading"><h2 data-relabel>A practice exam.<br/>With consequences.</h2><p>The lab is real. So are the changes you leave behind.</p></div><div class="process-flow"><article><h3><span class="mono">01</span>Build</h3><p>Build the RHEL 10 box once, from your own ISO.</p><Image src={home} width={800} widths={[320,480,800]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 44vw, 800px" format="webp" loading="lazy" alt="autorelabel home screen with exam choices"/></article><article><h3><span class="mono">02</span>Exam</h3><p>20 tasks. Start the clock when you are ready.</p><Image src={exam} width={800} widths={[320,480,800]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 44vw, 800px" format="webp" loading="lazy" alt="The timed RHCSA exam screen with tasks and node controls"/></article><article class="process-reboot"><Icon name="reboot"/><h3><span class="mono">03</span>Reboot</h3><p>Every node.<br/>Before grading.</p></article><article><h3><span class="mono">04</span>Results</h3><p>Checks, persistence warnings, and solutions.</p><Image src={results} width={800} widths={[320,480,800]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 44vw, 800px" format="webp" loading="lazy" alt="The real 258 out of 300 result and task 18 persistence warning"/></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="persistence-section"><div class="container persistence-grid"><h2 data-relabel>It worked.<br/><em>Then you rebooted.</em></h2><div><p>A firewall rule in memory can pass a check and disappear at the next boot. The pre-reboot pass records that difference. The post-reboot pass decides your score.</p><table class="persistence-table"><caption class="sr-only">Task 18 persistence example</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Task 18</th><th scope="col">Before</th><th scope="col">After</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Service enabled</th><td class="check-mark">✔</td><td class="check-mark">✔</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">SELinux port label</th><td class="check-mark">✔</td><td class="check-mark">✔</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Port reachable</th><td class="check-mark">✔</td><td class="check-mark check-mark--bad">✘</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Points</th><td>20 / 20</td><td>13.33 / 20</td></tr></tbody></table><a class="text-link" href="#reboot-result">Try the before/after switch ↑</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="simulation-section room--night"><div class="container simulation-grid"><div><h2 data-relabel>Try the first<br/>thing you’ll forget.</h2><p>Resetting a root password takes more than a new password. Walk through the boot interruption and find out why this project has its name.</p><p class="small muted">A short browser exercise. It does not run commands on your computer.</p></div><div class="simulation" data-simulation><div class="terminal-bar"><span>node2 · console exercise</span><button type="button" class="text-button" data-sim-reset>Reset</button></div><div class="sim-log" role="log" tabindex="0" aria-label="Console exercise output" aria-live="polite" aria-relevant="additions" data-sim-log><p>GRUB menu. Interrupt the boot to reset root’s password.</p></div><div class="sim-action"><p data-sim-prompt>Press e to edit the boot entry.</p><div class="button-row" data-sim-actions></div><form data-sim-form class="sim-command-form"><label class="sr-only" for="sim-command">Type the next command</label><div class="search-field"><span aria-hidden="true">#</span><input id="sim-command" type="text" data-sim-command autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Type the command, then Enter"/></div><button type="submit" class="btn btn--secondary">Run</button></form><button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" data-sim-show>Show me <Icon name="play"/></button></div><p class="sim-status" role="status" data-sim-status></p></div></div></section>
  <section class="feature-section container"><div class="section-title"><h2 data-relabel>What’s inside.</h2><p>The lab, the clock, and the checks.<br/>The details matter.</p></div><dl class="feature-ledger">{features.map(([title,description])=><div><dt>{title}</dt><dd>{description}</dd></div>)}</dl><a class="text-link" href={href('/how-it-works/')}>Follow the exam pipeline <Icon name="arrow"/></a></section>
  <section class="demo-section room--night"><div class="container"><div class="section-title"><h2 data-relabel>See the real thing.</h2><p>From the home screen to the results.<br/>The terminal interface, as it runs.</p></div><div class="video-frame" data-demo><div class="terminal-bar"><span>autorelabel · demo</span><span>RHEL 10</span></div><video width="1280" height="720" controls playsinline preload="none" poster={href('/media/demo-poster.avif')} aria-label="autorelabel demonstration" aria-describedby="demo-description"><source data-src={href('/media/demo-720.webm')} type="video/webm"/><source data-src={href('/media/demo-720.mp4')} type="video/mp4"/><p><a href={href('/media/demo-720.mp4')}>Watch the MP4 demo</a></p></video><button type="button" class="video-play btn" data-video-play data-cursor="play"><Icon name="play"/>Play demo</button><p class="sr-only" role="status" data-video-status></p></div><p class="video-description small muted" id="demo-description">This silent demo introduces the local RHEL 10 lab, showing the RHCSA utility server and two exam nodes, then RHCE’s control and managed nodes. A timed exam opens Task 18, serving a website on a non-standard port. The clock advances, and every node reboots before grading. The web service and SELinux checks pass, but the utility server cannot reach the page. The result is 258 out of 300, above the 210 pass mark. A final console sequence resets root’s password and runs <code>touch /.autorelabel</code>: forgetting that marker after <code>rd.break</code> prevents login.</p></div></section>
  <section class="platform-section container" id="platforms"><div class="section-title"><h2 data-relabel>Runs on your<br/>Linux machine.</h2><p>Bring your own RHEL 10 DVD.<br/>The box is built once, offline.</p></div><div class="prose" set:html={platforms.html}/><a class="btn" href={href('/start/')} data-magnetic>Check the requirements <Icon name="arrow"/></a></section>
  <section class="comparison-section container" id="comparison"><h2 data-relabel>How it compares.</h2><div class="prose comparison-prose" set:html={comparison.html}/></section>
  <section class="final-call room--night"><div class="container"><h2 data-relabel>Your next exam<br/>starts here.</h2><div><CommandBlock id="final-clone" commands={cloneCommands}/><a class="btn" href={href('/start/')} data-magnetic>Get started <Icon name="arrow"/></a><a class="text-link" href={href('/tasks/')}>Browse all {counts.total} task titles ↗</a></div></div></section>
</main>
</Layout>
